{"name":"Sour Lime","hex":"#acc326","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of acidity.","Made rancid by fermentation, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sensation of a sour taste.","A drink made with whiskey, lemon or lime juice and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour"},{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lime (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"A lime is the fruit of several species of citrus, most of which are hybrids within the genus Citrus. Limes are generally small, round to oval fruits with green flesh and skin and a distinctly sour taste due to their high citric acid content. They are widely cultivated in tropical and subtropical regions for culinary, medicinal, and ornamental purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Lime_Blossom.jpg/330px-Lime_Blossom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(fruit)"},{"title":"Sourness","blocks":[{"text":"Sourness, also known as sour, is a basic taste sensation perceived through hydrogen ions from acidic compounds interacting with taste bud receptors, and it can also refer to an unpleasant or acidic quality in taste, disposition, or tone. It is a warning sign for potentially spoiled food, though it is balanced in some food products by sweetness, and it is associated with a low pH."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lemon_with_white_background.jpg/330px-Lemon_with_white_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourness"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Citrus_hystrix_dsc07772.jpg/500px-Citrus_hystrix_dsc07772.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Citrus_hystrix_dsc07772.jpg/1280px-Citrus_hystrix_dsc07772.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Citrus_hystrix_dsc07772.jpg/500px-Citrus_hystrix_dsc07772.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kaffir lime fruit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACitrus_hystrix_dsc07772.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Essig-1.jpg/500px-Essig-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Essig-1.jpg/1280px-Essig-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Essig-1.jpg/500px-Essig-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","